	'k02d4482d' => 'Contact us',
	'k04118439' => 'Find clear answers to common questions about our application requirements, fee structure, customer contact protocols, and settlement processes. Every question is answered plainly with full operational transparency.',
	'k05b351c6' => 'No monthly fee. No minimum.',
	'k06e02b05' => 'Felipe Duarte · Duarte Bakehouse in Lyon',
	'k0c4f7d19' => 'Founded 2019 in Rotterdam',
	'k0cbd6cbb' => 'Design studios, technical consultants, and corporate staging providers routinely manage payroll and contractor expenses while waiting 60 days for enterprise clients to settle invoices. Azuke Finance supports service firms by advancing completed project milestones backed by client sign-off. This immediate liquidity ensures you can pay specialist freelancers, settle subcontractor invoices on schedule, and invest in project delivery without enduring the stress of commercial payment delays.',
	'k0f333165' => 'Upon confirmation, we transfer ninety percent of the invoice value directly to your business IBAN on the next working day. If approved before 13:00 CET, you can select our optional same-day payout for €25. When your customer pays the invoice on their agreed terms, we remit the remaining ten percent balance to you, deducting our 1.4 percent funding fee for the first thirty days. Apply in 3 minutes →',
	'k0f6d200d' => 'These terms govern the provision of invoice factoring and advance funding services by Azuke Finance B.V. By submitting an application or invoice for funding, you agree to these clear commercial conditions.',
	'k102a72d2' => 'Get in touch with our team in Rotterdam for assistance with invoice submissions, onboarding questions, or partner inquiries. We are available every working day during standard European business hours.',
	'k105852ec' => 'If your company is incorporated within the European Union, you do not need to wait for early access expansion. Our standard funding platform is fully operational today for EU businesses trading for at least six months. You can immediately submit commercial B2B invoices between €1,000 and €150,000 with proof of delivery to receive a 90% advance the next working day. Apply in 3 minutes →',
	'k137f2460' => 'Thank you for submitting your invoice to Azuke Finance B.V. We have received your documentation and our underwriting team in Rotterdam will reply within one working day.',
	'k1699d4f2' => 'Receive ninety percent the next working day',
	'k16ca97f7' => 'Information collected and purposes of processing',
	'k182da1bb' => 'When your customer remits full payment for the funded invoice, Azuke Finance deducts the accrued funding fee and releases the remaining balance to your business IBAN within one working day. In the event of prolonged debtor dispute or non-payment, the terms of the assigned invoice agreement govern recourse procedures. These terms are governed exclusively by the laws of the Netherlands, with the competent court in Rotterdam having primary jurisdiction. Apply in 3 minutes →',
	'k199e19b8' => 'Our principles of transparent financing',
	'k1e113809' => 'Review timelines and working hours',
	'k1e3c5956' => 'Maren Holt operates Holt Paper Goods, a sustainable packaging workshop based in Antwerp. When a regional retail chain placed an €8,600 packaging order on standard 45-day payment terms, Maren needed immediate liquidity to order fresh reels of recycled board for her next scheduled production run. Waiting six weeks for payment would have forced her to pause workshop machinery. By submitting the delivery note to Azuke Finance, Maren received a 90% cash advance the next working day, paying for her raw materials the very same week and keeping production running without interruption.',
	'k20848d9a' => 'Azuke Finance B.V. was established to provide small European suppliers with calm, transparent invoice funding. We believe businesses that have fulfilled their contracts deserve prompt access to the revenue they have earned.',
	'k2276f9a3' => 'Alternative submission methods and underwriting hours',
	'k237e3407' => 'Email your invoice',
	'k23f2360e' => 'Online application details and submission',
	'k258d203b' => 'Predictable financing for independent businesses',
	'k2aaa6a4a' => 'Apply · 3 min',
	'k2ac7abb0' => 'Our pricing structure is transparent, fixed, and free from hidden administrative charges. You only pay a simple funding fee on the specific invoices you choose to finance.',
	'k30cb9ba1' => 'Before beginning our three-minute application, ensure you have three essential items ready: your registered company number, your official business bank account IBAN, and a single completed B2B invoice between €1,000 and €150,000. The invoice must be accompanied by signed proof of fulfillment, such as a customer-signed delivery receipt, freight consignment note, or signed service sign-off sheet. Having these digital documents ready enables our underwriting team to evaluate your submission immediately without unnecessary correspondence or administrative delays.',
	'k386d0923' => 'Within one working day, our team contacts your customer by email to verify the invoice value and confirmed payment terms. Your customer receives a straightforward, polite notification verifying that the goods or services were satisfactorily delivered and noting the payment account details for invoice settlement. We maintain professional, respectful communications so your valuable trade relationships remain completely undisturbed. Most corporate accounts payable departments are familiar with standard assignment verifications, allowing the confirmation process to complete smoothly and without unnecessary friction or operational delays.',
	'k39e61d57' => 'For',
	'k3a031b3b' => 'Haringvliet 92, Rotterdam',
	'k3acc0b58' => 'Our underwriting review process',
	'k3b6c2b4c' => 'Terms of Service',
	'k3d9c4e94' => 'These illustrative cases reflect the practical working reality small European suppliers face every week. When you deliver high-quality goods and services, waiting months for trade settlement should never jeopardize your daily operations. Azuke Finance provides reliable working capital against verified invoices between €1,000 and €150,000, giving independent business owners the clarity and financial stability needed to grow sustainably. Apply in 3 minutes →',
	'k3e87d87e' => 'If you need to supplement your application with updated delivery receipts, or if you have questions regarding the confirmation process, our supplier relations lead Jonas Weber and customer support lead Amara Okoye are available to help. You can call our Rotterdam office directly at +31 10 555 0192 or email us at hello@azuke.example. We are located at Haringvliet 92, 3011 TG Rotterdam, Netherlands, and are always ready to assist.',
	'k3f34aae6' => 'To qualify for invoice funding with Azuke Finance, your business must be an EU-registered enterprise that has been trading actively for at least six months. We fund business-to-business commercial invoices with values ranging from €1,000 to €150,000 where goods or services have been fully delivered and verified by a signed delivery note or formal completion document. We do not fund consumer B2C invoices or advance payments for unperformed work. Apply in 3 minutes →',
	'k43041d1a' => 'Strict data privacy and European confidentiality',
	'k47e8426f' => 'Expansion',
	'k486456dc' => 'Contacting our team while your review is underway',
	'k4d458093' => 'We operate without complex legal covenants, surprise administrative deductions, or aggressive collection tactics. Every fee is stated openly before you confirm an advance: 1.4% for the first 30 days, 0.7% per further 15 days, and an absolute fee cap of 4.2%. We respect the trade relationships you have built, treating your customers with courtesy and professionalism throughout the confirmation and settlement stages. Apply in 3 minutes →',
	'k4e211a94' => 'Our supplier relations lead, Jonas Weber, works closely with workshops, wholesalers, and service businesses to ensure our funding facilities integrate smoothly with their delivery cycles. For ongoing operational assistance, account management, or debtor settlement queries, Amara Okoye leads customer support. Both Jonas and Amara work alongside co-founders Ines Vercauteren and Tomás Aldana to deliver dependable, personal service without automated call menus or detached outsourced support desks.',
	'k4e4e9094' => 'For immediate inquiries regarding active applications or funding status, telephone our Rotterdam desk at +31 10 555 0192 during standard business hours. For general company questions, partnership proposals, or introductory information, email hello@azuke.example. If you are submitting invoice documents, delivery notes, and corporate registration details for review, send your files directly to apply@azuke.example. We reply to all incoming business correspondence within one working day.',
	'k4ed95a91' => 'Wholesale suppliers and distributors',
	'k51359e8b' => 'Policy',
	'k52ea5623' => 'We collect information necessary to perform invoice underwriting, anti-money laundering compliance, and funding disbursements. This includes company registration numbers, business IBAN accounts, billing addresses, contact details of authorized company officers, submitted commercial invoices, and delivery fulfillment proofs. We process this information exclusively to assess credit risk, confirm delivery with your commercial debtors, execute bank transfers, and fulfill statutory accounting obligations under Dutch and European law. We do not engage in automated profiling or sell corporate data to third parties.',
	'k5405d8a9' => 'Frequently Asked Questions',
	'k543fca97' => 'Submitting an application takes approximately three minutes through our online portal. You only need your registered company number, your business bank account IBAN, and primary contact details. We do not ask for extensive historical business forecasts, personal director debentures, or lengthy administrative disclosures. There is no account setup fee, no recurring monthly subscription, and no ongoing volume commitment required to maintain an active profile. Once your basic business details are entered, your account profile is established, and you can immediately proceed to submit your first invoice for funding consideration.',
	'k5451b5ec' => 'Supplier relations and customer support',
	'k5538ac65' => 'Early Access and International',
	'k555c7cae' => 'Back to the home page',
	'k55cf5ac9' => 'Upload one invoice with proof of delivery',
	'k56752403' => 'Maren Holt · Holt Paper Goods in Antwerp',
	'k5c678193' => 'Mon–Fri 8:30–17:30 CET · +31 10 555 0192 · hello@azuke.example',
	'k61a7e35c' => 'Eligibility requirements',
	'k637fce46' => 'How It',
	'k64a01f5c' => 'Customer settlement and governing jurisdiction',
	'k65da470b' => 'When your customer pays the invoice according to their agreed trade terms, we immediately process the final settlement. We deduct our single funding fee—1.4% for the first 30 days, or the applicable rate based on payment timing—and transfer the remaining balance directly to your business IBAN. You receive an automated settlement statement detailing the exact figures. If you have questions during this period, our Rotterdam team is available Monday to Friday from 8:30 to 17:30 CET. Apply in 3 minutes →',
	'k6607ba4a' => 'Select a completed commercial invoice issued to an EU-based business customer with a value between €1,000 and €150,000. Upload a clear digital copy of the invoice alongside its corresponding proof of fulfillment, such as a signed delivery note, a confirmed bill of lading, or a counter-signed work completion certificate. Our underwriting team relies on evidence that goods have been received or services completed rather than relying solely on your balance sheet history. You decide exactly which invoices to fund, with complete control over your cash flow.',
	'k682889d0' => 'Funding',
	'k6839e357' => 'Azuke Finance B.V. was founded in 2019 with our headquarters located at Haringvliet 92, 3011 TG Rotterdam, Netherlands. Our name derives from the concept of azuke, meaning to entrust or hand over for safekeeping. We established the company after seeing independent workshops and manufacturers struggle under standard thirty to sixty day corporate payment terms. Traditional factoring providers imposed burdensome whole-turnover contracts and hidden management charges. We created a calm, transparent alternative designed specifically to safeguard the liquidity and independence of small European suppliers.',
	'k68ebca6b' => 'Small manufacturing workshops, bespoke packaging converters, and industrial print studios frequently encounter tight working capital constraints. When producing large custom orders for corporate clients, you must purchase cardboard, metal, textiles, or ink weeks before delivery, yet customer trade terms often require 30 to 45 days for invoice payment. By advancing 90% of your confirmed commercial invoice the day after delivery, Azuke Finance allows you to immediately restock raw materials and accept new customer contracts without waiting on slow payment cycles.',
	'k692b45ad' => 'Apply online in three minutes',
	'k6b2b5614' => 'Journal',
	'k6ce3bdc3' => 'Questions',
	'k6d436df4' => 'Applying takes approximately three minutes online. You only need your registered company number, your corporate IBAN, and direct contact details. When submitting an invoice for funding, you must upload the commercial invoice along with verifiable proof of delivery, such as a signed delivery note, consignment note, or signed completion certificate. Invoices must be issued to an EU business customer and carry a value between €1,000 and €150,000. There are no application fees, setup charges, or requirement to submit historical financial forecasts.',
	'k7291992c' => 'When do I receive the remaining ten percent balance of my invoice?',
	'k72fa60de' => 'How we make funding decisions',
	'k75ead19c' => 'Back to the start',
	'k798d9007' => 'In the standard course of invoice funding, our underwriting team contacts your business customer by email to verify invoice authenticity and goods delivery. This verification involves sharing the specific invoice number, transaction value, and designated payment remittance details. We do not disclose broader financial records or details of other customers. Outside of debtor verification, payment settlement banks, and mandatory legal compliance audits, we do not share your company data with any external commercial entities.',
	'k7aac0b09' => 'Fee predictability and settlement cap',
	'k7b8af977' => 'Works',
	'k802ef381' => 'Contact Azuke',
	'k8701fce1' => 'Advance payments, fee structures, and caps',
	'k8713773e' => 'What information and documents do I need to apply?',
	'k88260c57' => 'Azuke Finance B.V. is based in the maritime heart of Rotterdam. You can reach our office at Haringvliet 92, 3011 TG Rotterdam, Netherlands. Our team is active Monday through Friday from 8:30 to 17:30 CET. Whether you are an existing supplier checking a payment status or a new workshop evaluating invoice funding for an upcoming corporate contract, we welcome direct communication and provide specific, practical answers to your operational questions.',
	'k891bf579' => 'We are preparing to expand Azuke Finance beyond the European Union into adjacent European markets. Register your interest to access invoice funding as soon as onboarding launches in your jurisdiction.',
	'k8b475d9d' => 'We handle your business and financial data with utmost rigor under European data protection standards. Your company details, client contracts, and bank records are encrypted and utilized solely for underwriting verification, fraud prevention, and invoice settlement. We never sell, trade, or share your proprietary commercial information with external marketing organizations or non-affiliated third parties. You maintain full ownership of your commercial data throughout our engagement. Apply in 3 minutes →',
	'k8d61274b' => 'Your application has entered our review queue at our Rotterdam headquarters. Priya Raman, our underwriting lead, together with our credit team, will examine your submitted commercial invoice and proof of delivery. We verify company registration details, confirm the delivery documentation, and prepare our formal funding terms. We focus directly on the completed transaction rather than requesting exhaustive historical business forecasts, ensuring an efficient, objective, and calm evaluation process from start to finish.',
	'k8df7b2e7' => 'You see one fee before you accept, and it is charged once per invoice.',
	'k8e975549' => 'Submit your business details and upload one completed commercial invoice in approximately three minutes. Our team in Rotterdam reviews submissions within one working day.',
	'k8fee3ff7' => 'Invoice confirmation with your customer',
	'k9304542a' => 'Our simple application requires five core pieces of information: company name, registered company number, business email address, direct telephone number, and the exact face value of your commercial invoice. You do not need to upload personal financial statements, multi-year business projections, or balance sheet histories. After entering these details and attaching your invoice and delivery documentation, submit the form for immediate review. There is no application fee and no obligation to proceed until you accept our formal funding offer.',
	'k93d411b1' => 'What to prepare before starting your application',
	'k940150a0' => 'Terms of',
	'k95df9473' => 'Debtor verification and limited third-party disclosure',
	'k97efba81' => 'Invoice eligibility and legal assignment',
	'k99193498' => 'Felipe Duarte runs Duarte Bakehouse, an artisanal wholesale bakery in Lyon supplying hospitality venues across the region. When landing a major contract with a hotel group, Felipe issued a €3,200 invoice with 30-day payment terms. Facing a surge in holiday pastry orders, he required immediate working capital to purchase bulk flour, dairy, and seasonal ingredients. Azuke Finance funded 90% of the invoice value within twenty-four hours of verification, allowing Felipe to cover essential ingredient purchases for the holiday run without depleting his operating reserves.',
	'k996a9f80' => 'Our team evaluates submissions Monday through Friday between 8:30 and 17:30 CET. If you submitted your invoice during standard working hours, you can expect an initial response and term sheet by the following working day. If approved before 13:00 CET, you will have the option to select same-day payout for a €25 fee, or standard disbursement of your 90% advance on the next working day directly to your registered business IBAN.',
	'k99b52a41' => 'Wholesale bakeries, food producers, and component distributors routinely supply hotel chains, supermarkets, and regional enterprises on standard 30-day terms. Meeting sudden spikes in product demand requires immediate cash outlays for bulk flour, packaging supplies, and logistics transport. Instead of exhausting bank overdrafts or declining substantial purchase orders due to tied-up capital, wholesalers use Azuke Finance to unlock funds from delivered batches within one working day, keeping operations moving smoothly throughout seasonal peaks.',
	'k9d5c6b9e' => 'Frequently Asked',
	'ka0568977' => 'Sun-hee Park directs Park Print Studio, a specialist textile printing workshop in Cologne. After completing a custom fabric printing commission for a major event agency, she billed an invoice of €21,000 on 60-day terms. Sun-hee relied on two freelance screen printers who required prompt payment upon project completion. Rather than carrying the payroll deficit for two months, Sun-hee uploaded the invoice and signed completion certificate to Azuke Finance. The advance arrived the following working day, enabling her to compensate both freelancers promptly and maintain loyal studio partnerships.',
	'ka2678e60' => 'From the journal: Closing the Thirty-Day Cash Gap: How European Small Suppliers Protect Working Capital →',
	'ka4704fd3' => 'The',
	'ka564e2a2' => 'Read how independent European suppliers use Azuke Finance to overcome thirty to sixty day payment terms and maintain operational momentum. These accounts illustrate how real businesses fund materials and payroll without waiting for corporate settlement.',
	'ka67deb07' => 'Upcoming expansion to the United Kingdom and Switzerland',
	'ka6d4cacb' => 'Pricing and',
	'kaa22f311' => 'Our Rotterdam office brings together experienced professionals dedicated to straightforward supplier finance. Ines Vercauteren serves as co-founder focusing on credit assessment, while Tomás Aldana serves as co-founder leading daily operations. Priya Raman directs our underwriting lead team, evaluating submitted invoices and fulfillment documentation. Jonas Weber manages supplier relations, working closely with business owners across Europe to understand their operational needs. Amara Okoye leads customer support, assisting clients with onboarding, account inquiries, and payment settlements during our regular office hours from Monday to Friday, 8:30 to 17:30 CET.',
	'kaabda4ec' => 'How It Works',
	'kac5bb077' => 'Received',
	'kacc2ce1c' => 'Azuke Finance B.V. respects your privacy and is committed to protecting your corporate and personal information. This policy explains how we collect, process, and safeguard your data under European data protection legislation.',
	'kae143c27' => 'We retain transaction records and customer identification documentation for the statutory duration required by Dutch financial regulations and tax codes, typically seven years following the completion of an invoice funding transaction. Under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), you retain the right to inspect, correct, or request restriction of processing of your personal information. To exercise any of these statutory rights, contact our Rotterdam office. Apply in 3 minutes →',
	'kb567115d' => 'Specialist service firms',
	'kb6e2bb78' => 'Within one working day of receiving your invoice, our underwriting team contacts your customer\'s accounts payable department by email. We politely confirm that the invoiced goods or services were delivered as agreed and note the designated payment details for invoice settlement. We never demand immediate accelerated payment or disrupt your commercial partnership. Corporate accounts payable teams regularly process standard assignment confirmations, and our correspondence is calm, professional, and discreet, preserving the trust you have established with your customer.',
	'kb75cb09f' => 'Who It\'s',
	'kb80f4489' => 'We protect your business margins by capping total funding costs at 4.2% of the invoice value, regardless of extended settlement delays by your debtor. The initial 1.4% fee covers the first thirty days, with 0.7% added for each subsequent 15-day period until the cap is reached. You always know the exact maximum cost before accepting an advance, ensuring predictable financial planning. Apply in 3 minutes →',
	'kb8a2c59c' => 'Makers and workshop producers',
	'kbcbc3a33' => 'About Azuke Finance',
	'kbf779b7a' => 'Advance your invoices with clarity',
	'kbfe72508' => 'We fund individual commercial invoices so European suppliers do not have to wait thirty to sixty days for customer payments. Here is how our four-stage funding process moves from your initial submission to final settlement.',
	'kc043231c' => 'If you prefer not to submit through our web form, you can send your company registration number, IBAN, and invoice documentation directly to apply@azuke.example. You can also telephone our Rotterdam team directly at +31 10 555 0192. Our office hours are Monday through Friday, 8:30 to 17:30 CET. Priya Raman and our underwriting specialists review every incoming file promptly, ensuring you receive a definitive response and terms offer within one working day of submission.',
	'kc2ba7e78' => 'Service',
	'kc482980d' => 'Finance',
	'kc5f29bb3' => 'Privacy',
	'kcb2f40da' => 'Eligible invoices must represent completed sales of physical goods or delivered commercial services to business debtors within the European Union, with face values between €1,000 and €150,000. Consumer B2C invoices and progress billings for uncompleted work are strictly excluded. When you accept our funding offer for a specific invoice, you execute a legal assignment of the underlying debt to Azuke Finance B.V., warranting that the invoice is undisputed, valid, and free from existing liens or competing pledges.',
	'kcb50e4a0' => 'Worked example: a €12,400 invoice',
	'kcb5ea1e2' => 'Scope of agreement and contracting parties',
	'kcbb37401' => 'Stories',
	'kccc98459' => 'Our funding fee is 1.4% of the total invoice value for the first 30 days following approval. If your customer pays after 30 days, a fee of 0.7% applies for each additional 15-day period, up to an overall fee cap of 4.2%. We advance 90% of the invoice value the next working day after approval. You do not pay anything out of pocket; our fee is deducted from the remaining 10% reserve balance only after your customer settles the invoice in full.',
	'kd0fbda98' => 'Page not found',
	'kd1e59a74' => 'By registering for our early access list, you ensure your business is notified the moment underwriting opens for suppliers in your region. Priority waitlist members will receive expedited onboarding, direct access to our underwriting lead Priya Raman, and guidance on preparing your initial invoices for rapid funding. We only require your business name, operating country, and work email address. We respect your inbox and will never send unsolicited marketing messages or third-party advertisements.',
	'kd200362a' => 'Immediate availability for European Union suppliers',
	'kd3931733' => 'Telephone and email channels',
	'kd53ac74d' => 'Azuke Finance currently provides invoice factoring for businesses registered across the European Union. However, small suppliers throughout the United Kingdom and Switzerland face identical working capital challenges when delivering goods to corporate buyers on 30 to 60-day credit terms. Co-founders Ines Vercauteren and Tomás Aldana are actively structuring cross-border compliance, legal assignment protocols, and currency clearing to introduce our calm, per-invoice funding framework to UK and Swiss suppliers in our next deployment phase.',
	'kd95b665a' => 'Sun-hee Park · Park Print Studio in Cologne',
	'kdd7a29a8' => 'About Azuke',
	'kdd950486' => 'Azuke Finance is built specifically for growing European suppliers who sell on trade credit to corporate customers. If you deliver physical goods or commercial services and wait thirty to sixty days for payment, our service closes the cash gap.',
	'ke0b8a037' => 'Who It\'s For',
	'ke498749f' => 'Application',
	'ke60e88db' => 'No monthly fees and no minimum volume',
	'ke60f8358' => 'Traditional commercial lenders evaluate small suppliers almost entirely through historical balance sheets, tax returns, and rigid credit scoring models that fail to reflect current business health. At Azuke Finance, we take a different approach. We look primarily at the completed commercial transaction: the verified delivery of goods or services, signed documentation, and the creditworthiness of your corporate B2B buyer. If you have completed the order and your customer is a reputable enterprise, you have earned your cash. This practical evaluation makes funding accessible to growing, resilient businesses.',
	'ke646c76e' => 'The data controller responsible for your personal and company information is Azuke Finance B.V., founded in 2019 and registered in the Netherlands. Our registered office is located at Haringvliet 92, 3011 TG Rotterdam, Netherlands. For all data protection inquiries, access requests, or regulatory questions regarding how we process your information, contact our designated privacy officer via email at hello@azuke.example or telephone +31 10 555 0192 during our office hours of Monday to Friday, 8:30 to 17:30 CET.',
	'ke9782e68' => 'Unlike traditional invoice factoring contracts that demand annual retainers, audit fees, or whole-ledger turnover commitments, Azuke Finance operates on a flexible, per-invoice basis. There is no monthly fee and no minimum volume requirement. You can fund a single invoice during a seasonal demand surge and choose not to use the service again for months. We believe small suppliers should retain complete sovereignty over their financing costs without being locked into rigid long-term financial agreements.',
	'kea4cadf1' => 'If you have delivered goods or services to an EU business customer and want to eliminate the thirty to sixty day payment delay, speak with us today. With 90% paid on the next working day, a fixed 1.4% fee for the first 30 days, and no recurring monthly charges, Azuke Finance provides the cash flow certainty your business requires. Apply in 3 minutes →',
	'kec136b44' => 'Supplier',
	'kef936bf8' => 'Our Rotterdam headquarters and office hours',
	'kf1cea43e' => 'Join our priority onboarding waitlist',
	'kf62269a0' => 'Apply for Invoice',
	'kf631fcaa' => 'Azuke Finance operates with a straightforward fee structure published openly for every business. Setting up an account and submitting an application costs €0, with no monthly maintenance fees and no minimum invoice volume. When an invoice between €1,000 and €150,000 is approved, we advance 90% of the face value on the next working day. Our funding fee is 1.4% of the invoice value for the first 30 days. If your customer requires more time to pay, each further 15 days costs 0.7% of the invoice, up to an absolute fee cap of 4.2%. An optional same-day payout is available for €25 when approval occurs before 13:00 CET.',
	'kf79b8495' => 'Data retention periods and statutory rights',
	'kf7fa0ced' => 'How are funding fees calculated and when are they deducted?',
	'kf8cfeec0' => 'Transparent fee schedule',
	'kf9aef81b' => 'Consider an invoice for €12,400 issued on standard 30-day payment terms. Once approved, you receive an advance of €11,160, representing 90% of the invoice value, delivered to your bank account on the next working day. When your customer settles the full €12,400 invoice at the end of thirty days, we deduct our 1.4% funding fee of €173.60. The remaining €1,066.40 is immediately released to your business bank account. You access the majority of your cash right away to purchase materials or pay staff, with no unexpected deductions or compounding interest.',
	'kf9faf5ae' => 'The Azuke team',
	'kfa2ead69' => 'Privacy Policy',
	'kfcce73c0' => 'Upon debtor verification, Azuke Finance advances 90% of the invoice face value to your business IBAN on the next working day, or the same day for an additional €25 fee if approved before 13:00 CET. The funding fee is fixed at 1.4% of the invoice value for the first 30 days, plus 0.7% for each additional 15-day period up to an absolute cap of 4.2%. There are no recurring monthly maintenance charges, application fees, or minimum turnover requirements.',
	'kfd278915' => 'Join the waitlist',
	'kff392f73' => 'These terms constitute a legally binding agreement between your registered business and Azuke Finance B.V., an enterprise founded in 2019 with its principal office at Haringvliet 92, 3011 TG Rotterdam, Netherlands. Azuke Finance provides selective invoice advance facilities for commercial B2B invoices. By registering an account profile or submitting an invoice through our web platform, email, or telephone, you confirm that you are an authorized representative of an active EU-registered enterprise trading for at least six months.',
